+### User-approved table interpretation: alliance defense
+
+**Adopted for this table on November 5, 2026:** An active strength-2 local alliance can successfully defend a strength-1 Crisis by exhausting the whole alliance piece. Apply the normal successful-defense results: clear the attacked region’s unrest; the actual Commander gains one trophy (Military Affairs/Chairman substitutes gain or lose none); if this defeats a normal primary Invasion, remove one attacker tower if possible. The exhausted alliance cannot be used again that turn.
+
+**Authority and scope:** This is the user’s accepted interpretation, based on local alliances being Army pieces; it is **not a publisher/designer ruling**. It settles this stated case for play here. It does not establish a general greater-than-or-equal rule or resolve other excess-strength cases. Official verification remains pending.
+
 **Source boundary:** This is a playable procedural summary used with board and cards. Printed prize/track/scenario values and individual law, spouse, promise and failure effects remain authoritative. Crown rules and optional draft setup are outside scope.
 
